libpmg-rs-perl (0.8.5) trixie; urgency=medium

  * apt: history: tell whether a transaction without end time is still running
    or got interrupted. As APT runs one transaction at a time, only the
    newest one can still be running, which it is if the process holding the
    lock of the dpkg frontend started before it. If that cannot be told, the
    state stays open as before.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 03:48:07 +0100

libpmg-rs-perl (0.8.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * apt: update changelogs:
    - show that the repository provides no changelog for packages of
      repositories without a changelog location, like most of those of third
      parties, instead of reporting them as missing from the package lists
      and counting them as failed in the daily prefetch.
    - keep the cached changelogs if resolving their locations fails, for
      example at the time limit, and show APT's error for failures that
      are not about a package, like a broken list of sources.
    - write the cache markers atomically, so that a daily prefetch running at
      the same time cannot empty the cache.

  * apt: terminal output: ignore the parameters of underline colors instead of
    taking them as styles of their own, which could, for example, make text
    bold.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:39:36 +0100

libpmg-rs-perl (0.8.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * access log: add bindings for paging through and following the API
    access log of the node, including its rotated and compressed copies,
    and for request statistics of a time range. Callers can have the
    values of query parameters redacted, as clients can pass passwords
    in them.

  * apt: add bindings for the history of past APT transactions, with their
    package changes and terminal output, so the update history of a node
    can be shown through the API.

  * apt: add bindings for the changelogs of an installed package, of all
    package changes of a transaction and of all pending updates. The
    changelogs of pending updates get downloaded in one APT run and cached,
    and the cache can be filled after refreshing the package lists, so
    showing them usually needs no download.

  * drop the notification bindings, which PMG does not use and which moved
    to libpve-rs-perl, so the library no longer pulls in their dependencies.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:33:50 +0100

libpmg-rs-perl (0.8.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * fix detecting the legacy `pmgtest` deb822 component that PMG 8 wrote out
    (PMG 9 standardized to `pmg-test`), so already-configured test
    repositories on upgraded hosts get recognized rather than offered as still
    addable. The next write through the repository API rewrites the component
    to the canonical `pmg-test` form, fixing the on-disk file; the legacy path
    is no longer hosted on download.proxmox.com and would otherwise 404 on the
    next apt update.

  * fix adding a standard PMG repository through the API always writing a new
    sources file instead of just enabling an already-configured one, due to a
    hardcoded internal PBS product reference.

  * rebuild against proxmox-apt 1.0.1 / proxmox-apt-api-types 3.0; the APT API
    boundary now takes a typed HostProduct enum, and the canonicalize-on-write
    fix lands here via the 1.0.1 point release.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Wed, 20 May 2026 03:15:57 +0200

